From: Ben Bangert <100193+bbangert@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: rk8xx: allow boards to opt out of PMIC restart

On RK809/RK817 the driver restarts the board with the PMIC's DEV_RST
bit, at a higher priority than PSCI. That power-cycles the SoC and
clears the PMU GRF reboot mode register, so "reboot loader" and
"reboot recovery" never reach the vendor U-Boot on the Pastigio
FRAME156. The stock vendor kernel restarts through PSCI, which keeps
the register. Add "rockchip,no-pmic-restart" to skip the PMIC restart
handler; power-off still goes through the PMIC.

---
--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
@@ -881,6 +881,14 @@
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
 					     "failed to register poweroff handler\n");
 
+		/*
+		 * A PMIC reset power-cycles the SoC and clears the reboot
+		 * mode register in the PMU GRF, so boards whose bootloader
+		 * acts on that register restart through PSCI instead.
+		 */
+		if (device_property_read_bool(dev, "rockchip,no-pmic-restart"))
+			return 0;
+
 		switch (rk808->variant) {
 		case RK809_ID:
 		case RK817_ID:
